    {
      "id": 235004,
      "name": "",
      "username": "fjur",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/{size}/4849_2.png",
      "created_at": "2021-02-06T16:02:35.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Unload and Eruption (and all other mass Attacks) do&nbsp;not necessarily need to be uncontrollable or controllable, though. It really depends on the fiction. If the fiction of the Attact says it's uncontrollable, then it is. But if the Attack's fiction says that the Attack can hit all enemies in a scene and no allies, then so be it.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>A fireball would hit everything in the&nbsp;area.</li>\n\t<li>Vines sprouting out of the ground to strangle foes would Attack only your enemies.</li>\n\t<li>Unloading a machine gun could hit any number of allies or enemies in an area.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Hope this helps!</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:11:13.893Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
